WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:21.160
November 3rd, 1957 2:30 AM UTC

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.370
Altitude 5,000... 6,000!

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.710
First stage jettison complete.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.170
Temperature stabilized at 20C.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:25.960
Successful launch of Artificial Satellite Parusnyĭ Two

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.880
Heart rate: three times normal.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.180
Respiratory rate:
four times normal. No issues.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.890
Leaving the atmosphere.
We're officially zero-G.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.890
Orbit insertion successful!

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.060
Vital signs normal. It's alive in space!

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:50.030
That day, an animal flew in space
for the first time in history.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.400
Soyuz Zirnitra Sotsialisticheskikh Respublik
Satellite Orbits the Globe for a Week!

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:59.040
The UZSR's incredible feat
shocked the entire world.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.280
Maly the Space Dog

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:06.420
Zirnitra Union
Arctic Air Force Base

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.550
Someday, I'll go!

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:20.930
Lilitto
Anival Village

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:32.990
Sinus Iridum, Palus Somni,
Mare Tranquillitatis...

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:44.540
In an era where humans
have yet to reach the cosmos,

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:51.130
this is the story of a boy and girl who
risk their lives for their love of space.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:15.400
Irina: The Vampire Cosmonaut

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.940
September, 1945
World War ends

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.190
After the World War
which divided the globe,

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.440
the east's Zirnitra Union

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.610
and west's United Kingdom of Arnack

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:44.910
set their sights on space,
which was yet unclaimed.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:47.750
The UZSR moved first.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:55.010
On October 4th, 1957, the UZSR
launched the first satellite into orbit.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:54.040
October 4th, 1957 10:28 PM
First successful launch of artificial satellite

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:59.880
One month after, they put
the first animal into space.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.460
Here rests 'Maly the Space Dog'

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:04.310
The United Kingdom's response
exploded two seconds after launch.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:08.100
September 1959
The UZSR's Diana 2 lands on Moon

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:10.650
The UZSR was unstoppable.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.560
Diana 3 photographs far side of Moon

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:16.400
The UK triumphs at making burgers,
but the UZSR triumphs at lunar landings.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:16.480
Supreme Leader of the UZSR
Gergiev

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.280
<i>Newspaper The Istina</i>
'We Have Conquered Space'

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:23.200
Their dignity on the line,

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:28.290
the nations raced to claim
the first human spaceflight.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.370
<i>Arnack News</i>
'Send humans to space!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:34.250
The Nosferatu Project

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:46.010
October 10th, 1960 3:12 PM
Northern Zirnitra

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:53.100
Cosmonaut Lev Leps has returned home!

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.190
Who's a cosmonaut now?

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.900
You're just a reserve.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:02.280
In spirit, okay? In spirit...

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:02.360
Reserve Cosmonaut Candidate
Air Force Private Second Class, Lev Leps

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:27.470
Closed Administrative-
Territorial Formation
Space Research City 'LAIKA44'

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:37.400
Thank goodness. The trip's finally over.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.110
Hey, Lev!

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:43.410
What is it, sir?

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:46.240
Follow me. Comrade Chief wants to talk.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.320
Cosmonaut Training Center Director
Lt. Gen. Viktor

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:47.870
The Chief?

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.580
What'd you do now?

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.330
Nothing at all!

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:56.210
It's gotta be something. He wouldn't
come way out here for nothing.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.840
Was nice knowing you.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.630
Hurry up, Lev!

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.630
Yes, sir!

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:06.930
Long time no see.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.970
Space Research City 'LAIKA44' Development
Sector - Cosmonaut Training Center

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:12.430
I take it you're training hard to be
selected for the first, human spaceflight?

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:14.440
Yes, Comrade Chief!

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:19.480
Though after your incident, you were
demoted to a reserve candidate.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:25.490
Your marks are high, but presently,
there's zero chance that you're chosen.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:26.780
I understand that.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:34.210
But I have other uses for your talent.
I'm assigning you to a certain project.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:33.580
1st Design Bureau Chief
Slava Korovin

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.630
Huh? Yes, sir!

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:40.500
The Manned Spaceflight Project, "Mechta"

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.500
Manned Spaceflight Project: 'Mechta'

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:46.760
Our mission is the same, but the
Committee has added a new objective.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.390
Let's finish the UK off!

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:54.560
When we put a human in space,
I want it broadcast live to the world!

00:06:54.560 --> 00:07:00.690
A live broadcast? But if we fail,
we can't cover it up like we have before.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:05.360
Precisely. That presents us
with a huge problem.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.520
Isn't that right, Dr. Mozhaysky?

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:10.450
Head of Biomedical Laboratory
Dr. Mozhaysky

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:11.240
There're things a dog can't tell us:

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:16.670
Can people function in zero gravity?
Will seeing the globe break their spirit?

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:19.540
Our cosmonauts are like heroes.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:24.260
If one is hurt or killed during
the broadcast, it'll be a disaster.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:26.880
Biomedical Laboratory Annex
Animal Experimentation Institute

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:27.130
When we brought this up to the Committee,

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:31.510
they demanded we perform
an outrageous experiment.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:33.720
To use people?

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.640
Experimental subjects are mere objects.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:45.400
The Supreme Leader has given us the order.
If we fail, our lives may be forfeit.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:45.480
Top-Secret Plan: 'N Project'

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:47.530
What must I do?

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:48.570
Hmm?

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.410
I'm the subject, right?

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:56.540
You fool. If we sent you to space,
you'd be a full-fledged cosmonaut.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.210
Then who is?

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:01.330
Not a human, but a vampire.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.170
Vampire?

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.170
A Loathed, Cursed Species

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:10.550
Vampires are a rare species, isolated deep
in the mountains of UZSR territory.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:15.600
Most people have a terrifying image
of them from movies and novels,

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:18.060
but have never seen one.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:23.570
Lev was one of those people.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:22.440
Biomedical Laboratory Annex
Underground Solitary Confinement Cells

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:53.090
Come out of there.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.280
That girl's a vampire?

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:18.500
That's right. Tracking ID: N44.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:23.080
Though their species has
peculiar traits and abilities,

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:26.380
they're biologically close to humans.

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:29.970
Therefore, an ideal subject
for our experiment.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:35.100
They don't classify as humans,
so it won't count as human flight.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:38.060
And if she dies, it's an easy cover-up.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:45.060
Now then, Lev...

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:46.770
Yes, sir!

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.650
Your mission is as follows...

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.950
You have four objectives.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:10:01.830
One: for roughly two months until launch,
you're to monitor and train N44.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:07.290
Two: keep N44's identity
a secret from civilians.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:11.260
Irina Luminesk... Age 21?

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:10.380
Air Force Private Second Class
Irina Luminesk

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:15.260
Three: ensure N44 does not escape.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:15.880
Committee for State Security
AKA 'Delivery Crew'

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:20.810
Four: live in the adjacent room
to monitor N44 at all times.

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:23.480
Wait... I'm living here, too?

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:28.060
Your personal effects
were moved to the next cell.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.740
Stand up, N44.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:41.410
Lev, when you take her outside,
make sure to hide her ears.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.710
We can go outside?

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:50.050
Think of it like walking a dog so the
solitude doesn't bore you to death.

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:52.760
Well, I'll be on my way.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:54.630
I'm all on my own?

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:59.550
As if. You'll have a helper
well-versed in vampires.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.510
Anya!

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:06.350
She's young, but bright.
She'll fill you in on the details.

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:11.820
Nice to meet you!
I'm N44's health manager, Anya!

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:11.900
Biomedical Laboratory Researcher
Anya Simonyan

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:16.660
N-Nice to meet you.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:23.250
I think you know, but treat N44 like
an experimental subject--like an object.

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:24.250
Yes, sir!

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:33.510
My dreams are done for.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.590
May I continue now?

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.180
Yeah, sorry.

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:45.520
Vampires are weak against sunlight,
so training will last from dusk till dawn.

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:49.440
Meaning I've gotta sleep all day long?

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:53.530
By the way, does sunlight
turn 'em into ashes?

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.990
No! That's a myth!

00:11:55.990 --> 00:12:03.030
It'll just cause their skin to tingle,
but they do seem to get heatstroke easily.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:07.580
However, night vision
allows them to see in the dark.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.210
Yeah?

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:14.170
Lev, here's today's schedule.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:19.380
Meal, city tour, sleeping
until dusk tomorrow...

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:20.550
Meal?

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.060
Does she drink blood?

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:32.520
No, she'll have the same meals as you.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.770
Not blood?

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:40.950
No! The other candidates are
in the cafeteria, so go introduce her!

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:42.280
Roger that.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:48.040
Let's go, Irina. Put these on.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:50.500
Lev! You mustn't use her name!

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:53.840
I'll call her Irina
when we're around town.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:55.210
Why?

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:58.970
If I call her N44,
people will ask questions.

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:00.930
But, that's...

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.350
You look like a regular candidate now.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:12.980
IRINA: THE VAMPIRE COSMONAUT

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:28.040
About 9,000 people live
in this city doing space research.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:32.870
But it's not on the map
and they're not registered citizens.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:35.540
'Cuz space research is a national secret.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.710
Space Research City 'LAIKA44'
Residential Sector - Dormitory

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:41.880
Cafeteria

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:44.800
Here's the cafeteria.
I'll introduce you to everyone.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:49.560
Take off your hat. Might as well
show 'em right off the bat.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:03.610
This is N44, Irina Luminesk.
All right, guys?

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.950
Let's go.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:09.540
--What, her?
--Who's that?

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:10.990
Her ears are pointy.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:12.160
Fangs?

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.710
Does she bite?

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:16.290
She's got the vampire skin and eyes.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.370
Cosmonaut Candidate
Air Force Private Second Class, Roza Plevitskaya

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.260
She looks human.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:23.130
But she's a monster.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:30.810
I'll suck your blood!
I'll suck your blood!

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:35.650
Can it, Yustin.

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:36.940
Eh?

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:38.440
You're an idiot.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.740
Would you say that without backup?

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:50.660
I oughta--!

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.710
So tasteless. That's why I hate humans.

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:55.080
What?!

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.790
H-Hey...

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:03.380
She hates humans...

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:06.890
Hold on! Guys, just listen!

00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:12.560
She eats the same food as us.
Didn't Lt. Gen. Viktor tell you guys?

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:17.100
Welcome to the forefront
of space research!

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:17.940
What?

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:23.240
She devoted her life to helping us.
Let's be thankful!

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:21.020
Cosmonaut Candidate Air Force Private
Second Class, Mikhail Yashin

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:26.150
Mikhail...

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:30.030
Why don't we let Lev take over from here?

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.700
Yeah.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:32.950
Tsk!

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:40.710
Hey, where's our food?

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.710
Eh?

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.790
Milk?

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:48.890
You eat what humans do, right?

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:52.390
That's borscht--a Zirnitra specialty.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:57.020
Also, I was told to give you this.

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:56.890
Dorm Matron
Natalia

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.360
Milk?

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:01.520
Yup!

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:42.020
Not a Cute Dog

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:50.320
The residential sector has all sorts of
places--libraries, schools, restaurants...

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:53.070
Even a lake you can skate on in winter.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:59.660
What's up? Something wrong?

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:07.550
Don't look!

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:10.970
Stay back, human!

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:12.970
But, the cross...

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:17.930
Huh? What?

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:22.560
Did you read that that's our
weak point in a book or something?

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:25.360
So, you're okay?

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:28.990
It's all nonsense that humans made up.

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:31.660
Uh, what's that?

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:36.910
That's...

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.210
What is it?

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:45.630
Well, that's the grave
of the first dog in space, Maly.

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:49.840
You mourn the lives you treat
as objects? That's backwards.

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:53.550
It wasn't always this way.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:56.640
If anything, Maly was loved.

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:04.150
Three years ago, the regime demanded
the first animal spaceflight.

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:05.060
November 3rd, 1957
Artificial Satellite Parusnyĭ Two

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:10.900
Except, Maly's ship was incomplete
and wasn't built to return.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.780
But the regime's words were final.

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:16.070
Rapid heart rate and breathing.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:19.370
Engine cut-off. Ship is now zero-G.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:21.200
It's alive in space!

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:25.500
They achieved a historical feat, but...

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.590
Anomalies!

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:32.050
Internal temperature is rising! 42! 43C!

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:37.220
Due to the extreme heat,
Maly died in a few hours.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:42.890
A few hours? I read it flew
for a week in the paper!

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:44.850
Was that a lie?

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:47.440
I've said too much.

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:53.030
After that tragedy, it became an unwritten
rule to treat subjects like objects.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:19:01.870
Isn't that just running away
from the guilt?

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.370
Who knows?

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:11.630
I guess that makes you lucky--that I'm
a cursed species and not a cute dog.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:12.670
That's not--

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.340
It's fine.

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:18.010
I don't want some human's sympathy anyway.

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:24.060
Experimental subjects are mere objects.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.520
No. To me...

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:52.420
October 11th, 2:15 AM

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:54.460
Biomedical Laboratory Annex
Underground Solitary Confinement Cells

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:01.430
It's so damn cold.

00:20:12.070 --> 00:20:13.980
It's me. I'm coming in.

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:25.580
Are you cold? Want a blanket?

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:35.710
No, I'm not cold. Don't you know
my species handles cold just fine?

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:38.300
Oh, the weak against heat thing...

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:39.970
So leave already.

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:44.680
Sorry for not knowing.

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:53.900
And sorry for not stopping them from
saying mean things in the cafeteria.

00:20:56.110 --> 00:21:04.660
And, as for me... Sorry for treating
you like an experimental subject.

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:50.660
That guy and that Anya girl...

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:55.630
If they get orders to kill me,
they won't think twice about it.

00:21:55.630 --> 00:22:00.220
I won't let my guard down.
Humans can't be trusted.

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:51.030
Next Episode:
'The Path to Becoming a Cosmonaut'
